---
const title = 'Maxim';
// Positioning is deliberately scoped: a harness around an LLM, not a claim of
// biological fidelity, and not a claim that the substrate overrides the model.
// See docs/announcements/pymaxim_bio_update_suggestions.md in the pymaxim repo.
const tagline =
	'A bio-inspired LLM harness that carries experience-grounded memory, causal links, drives, and valence across sessions — without fine-tuning model weights.';
const description = tagline;
const ogImage = new URL('/og.png', Astro.site);
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>{title} — a bio-inspired LLM harness with persistent memory</title>
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="canonical" href={Astro.site} />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:url" content={Astro.site} />
		<meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
		<main id="main" data-pagefind-body>
			<section class="hero">
				<h1>Maxim</h1>
				<p class="tagline">{tagline}</p>
				<div class="install">
					<code id="install-cmd">pip install pymaxim</code>
					<button type="button" data-copy="pip install pymaxim" aria-label="Copy install command" hidden>
						Copy
					</button>
				</div>
				<nav class="links" aria-label="Project links">
					<a href="/getting-started/">Get started</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
					<a href="https://pypi.org/project/pymaxim/" rel="noopener">PyPI</a>
				</nav>
			</section>

			<section class="what" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
				<h2 id="what-heading">What's in it</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<h3>Embodied sensation</h3>
						<p>
							Agents perceive through a sensory layer instead of raw prompt stuffing — built to
							connect to real hardware like the Reachy robot as well as software environments.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Homeostatic drives</h3>
						<p>
							Internal state — energy, curiosity, social need — shifts what the agent attends to
							and chooses to do, the way physiological drives steer behavior.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Brain-modeled memory</h3>
						<p>
							Memory systems named after their biological counterparts (Hippocampus, NAc, EC, ATL,
							SCN) consolidate experience into a substrate that persists across sessions — no
							fine-tuning run required. The naming is design inspiration, not a claim of
							biological fidelity.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="scope">
					In the default path the LLM still decides. The substrate supplies
					experience-grounded context to that decision; it does not generally override the
					model's priors, and where it was tested against a deliberately wrong prior, the
					prior won. <a href="/research/experiments/substrate-primary-evidence/">What the
					evidence actually shows →</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="what" aria-labelledby="evidence-heading">
				<h2 id="evidence-heading">What's been demonstrated</h2>
				<p class="scope">
					Maxim is developed as a falsification-oriented research project. These are
					mechanism demonstrations at modest N, not competitive benchmarks. The
					<a href="/research/evidence/">evidence page</a> gives each result with the caveat
					that bounds it.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<h3>Learning to want: orienting taught through hunger relief</h3>
						<p>
							An infant with a hunger drive and no orient drive learned to turn toward its
							mother's voice because being fed relieved its hunger — and did not learn when fed
							on the same schedule without need, or not at all. Scripted and embodied, twelve
							seeds per arm, no LLM in the action path. One session; the credit only
							discriminates relief from no relief.
							<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/experiments/52_nurture.md" rel="noopener">Exp 52 →</a>
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Sensorimotor learning on real hardware</h3>
						<p>
							On a Reachy Mini, the substrate learned a closed-loop sound-orienting policy from
							scratch in about ten trials with no LLM in the action path, carried it across
							sessions, and merged two independently trained substrates into a working combined
							policy. Later arms extended this to <em>how far</em> to turn, not just which way.
							Magnitude claims from the pre-repair robot were re-validated on the repaired robot
							in August 2026 — one session, cross-session replication outstanding.
							<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/experiments/45_reachy_orient_live.md" rel="noopener">Exp 45 series →</a>
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Safe-vs-harmful discrimination without the LLM</h3>
						<p>
							With the language model removed from the action path entirely, the substrate learned
							from embodied pain to prefer a safe warmth source over a harmful one, and tracked the
							contingency when the two were swapped. Re-validated after a later refactor. The
							metric is saturated, so a passing re-run shows "not broken" rather than "not
							degraded".
							<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/experiments/42_substrate_primary_preference.md" rel="noopener">Exp 42 →</a>
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<h3>Where it didn't hold up</h3>
						<p>
							Carried substrate does <em>not</em> override a strong contrary LLM prior — tested
							across four frontier models and dominated in all of them. And the first embodied
							operant-orienting result was re-baselined onto a corrected apparatus: the caregiver
							effect survived, the learning gate did not, and the metric turned out to track phase
							alignment rather than skill — the fix became Exp 52 above.
							<a href="/research/cradle/">Exp 48, the apparatus case study →</a>
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="scope">
					The project keeps public ledgers of what is broken and what its instruments
					cannot resolve:
					<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/bugs/README.md" rel="noopener">known defects</a>,
					<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/limits/README.md" rel="noopener">measurement limits</a>,
					and the
					<a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim/blob/main/docs/plans/behavioral_graduation_candidates.md" rel="noopener">behavioral-claim ledger</a>.
					Every experiment is indexed on the <a href="/research/experiments/">experiments page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<footer>
			<p>
				Apache-2.0 · <a href="https://github.com/dennys246/Maxim" rel="noopener">pymaxim</a> ·
				<a href="/getting-started/">Docs</a>
			</p>
		</footer>

		<script>
			// Progressive enhancement: show the copy button only when JS + clipboard exist.
			const btn = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]');
			if (btn && navigator.clipboard) {
				btn.hidden = false;
				btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
					await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy ?? '');
					btn.textContent = 'Copied';
					setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = 'Copy'), 1500);
				});
			}
		</script>

		<style>
			:root {
				--bg: #fdfcfa;
				--fg: #1c1b1a;
				--muted: #5c5955;
				--accent: #1a7a63;
				--surface: #f1efeb;
				--border: #dedad4;
				color-scheme: light dark;
			}
			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
				:root {
					--bg: #151413;
					--fg: #ecebe8;
					--muted: #a3a09a;
					--accent: #4cc2a4;
					--surface: #201f1d;
					--border: #35332f;
				}
			}
			* {
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}
			/* Keyboard users land here first and can jump the header links.
			   Visually hidden until focused, matching the docs pages' behavior. */
			.skip-link {
				position: absolute;
				left: 0.5rem;
				top: -3rem;
				z-index: 10;
				padding: 0.5rem 0.85rem;
				background: var(--surface);
				color: var(--accent);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 0.375rem;
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: top 0.15s ease-in-out;
			}
			.skip-link:focus {
				top: 0.5rem;
			}
			body {
				margin: 0;
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
				font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}
			main {
				max-width: 44rem;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 1.25rem;
			}
			.hero {
				padding: 6rem 0 3rem;
				text-align: center;
			}
			h1 {
				font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 3.5rem);
				margin: 0 0 1rem;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			}
			.tagline {
				font-size: 1.125rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				max-width: 38rem;
				margin: 0 auto 2rem;
				text-wrap: balance;
			}
			.install {
				display: inline-flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.5rem;
				background: var(--surface);
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 0.5rem;
				padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}
			.install code {
				font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
				font-size: 0.95rem;
			}
			.install button {
				font: inherit;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				color: var(--accent);
				background: none;
				border: 1px solid var(--border);
				border-radius: 0.375rem;
				padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
				cursor: pointer;
			}
			.links {
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				justify-content: center;
				gap: 1.5rem;
			}
			.links a {
				color: var(--accent);
				font-weight: 500;
				text-decoration: none;
			}
			.links a:hover,
			.links a:focus-visible {
				text-decoration: underline;
			}
			.what {
				padding: 2rem 0 4rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
			}
			.what h2 {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
			}
			.what ul {
				list-style: none;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				display: grid;
				gap: 1.5rem;
			}
			.what h3 {
				margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}
			.scope {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.95rem;
			}
			.what a {
				color: var(--accent);
			}
			.what p {
				margin: 0;
				color: var(--muted);
			}
			footer {
				border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
				text-align: center;
				padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}
			footer a {
				color: var(--accent);
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
